# Appendix: Optimization Strategies for Virtual Credits

## 1. State Vector Manipulation

### 1.1. State Vector Construction

The core optimization is managing the state vector. In a stochastic environment, the state vector is the current probability distribution over actions. To maximize virtual credits, you must ensure the state vector remains stable during transitions.

**1.1.1. Entropy Biasing**

Entropy is the measure of disorder in a state vector. In a stochastic environment, high entropy means the system is uncertain. To stabilize the state vector, you bias the entropy toward a lower value.

**Algorithm:**
```
function entropy_bias(state) {
    // Calculate entropy of current state
    entropy = 0;
    for (i = 0; i < state.length; i++) {
        if (state[i] > 0) entropy += state[i];
    }
    entropy = entropy / state.length;
    // Bias the state vector toward lower entropy
    for (i = 0; i < state.length; i++) {
        if (state[i] > 0) state[i] = -state[i];
